  {
   "id": "wa_bluebird",
   "before": {
    "overview": "Overlooked classic: a corner system on the left of Right Gull that merges with it near the top. Traverse brushy ledges over the second tunnel to a pillar belay (with a burly 5.8 offwidth beneath), then the right-hand corner crack, which tightens and gets harder as it rises. Can be dirty."
   },
   "after": {
    "overview": "Overlooked classic: a clean corner crack left of Right Gull that joins it near the top. Skip the first ascent's start across the brushy ledges, because the top of the big leaning pillar there is detached and shifts. Instead go up Spring Fever, Winter Delight or Sufficiently Breathless, keep going to a newer bolted anchor above, and follow the right-hand crack as it widens from small gear to fingers and hands, with a thin crux just below a rest ledge two-thirds of the way up. Can be dirty."
   },
   "why": "SAFETY: overview moved off the original start (detached pillar) to the bolted start"
  },
